verdict.analysis:
Solution A is fundamentally more grounded because it leverages a "pull" model where customers self-select the discount during their visit, preventing the operational disaster of managing a subscription database. However, the critiques highlight significant flaws regarding cannibalization and the labor intensity of the "final hour." It is a better, albeit flawed, attempt at retail management compared to Solution B.

Solution B is highly impractical. The core fatal flaw is the "Fresh Anchor Item," which forces the bakery to sacrifice high-margin, full-price goods to subsidize the sale of leftovers, effectively cannibalizing the business's primary revenue stream. Additionally, the manual management of an SMS/WhatsApp list for subscription boxes in a high-stress retail environment is a recipe for operational failure and high legal risk regarding unlabelled, "blind" food items.

